civic-gads
==========

This product is a Civic-internal port of:

  Google Ads API Developer Assistant
  https://github.com/googleads/google-ads-api-developer-assistant
  Copyright 2025-2026 Google LLC
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0

Original work was authored by Google LLC for use with the Gemini CLI.
This port adapts the project for use as a Claude Code plugin and is
maintained by Civic Technologies, Inc. for internal use.

Significant port changes (2026):
  - Renamed GEMINI.md -> CLAUDE.md (and conversions/GEMINI.md -> conversions/CLAUDE.md).
  - Replaced gemini-extension.json with .claude-plugin/plugin.json.
  - Moved settings, hooks, commands, and skills from .gemini/ to .claude/.
  - Converted slash commands from .toml (description+prompt fields) to .md
    (YAML frontmatter + body) using $ARGUMENTS instead of {{args}}.
  - Replaced Gemini-specific tool references (run_shell_command, web_fetch,
    save_memory, replace, write_file, read_file, grep_search) with the
    Claude Code equivalents (Bash, WebFetch, auto-memory rule, Edit, Write,
    Read, Grep) throughout CLAUDE.md.
  - Replaced the SessionStart hook's `custom_vars` env-var injection with an
    `additionalContext` payload that instructs the agent on the deterministic
    venv path and GOOGLE_ADS_CONFIGURATION_FILE_PATH to prepend to Bash calls.
  - Removed Gemini-specific `~/.gemini/policies/ads_assistant.toml` policy
    management; the equivalent guardrail is encoded directly in CLAUDE.md
    as a "NO PERSISTENCE" rule against Claude Code's auto-memory system.
  - Pointed the upstream-version checker at a configurable URL via the
    CIVIC_GADS_REMOTE_PLUGIN_JSON_URL env var (skips silently when unset).
  - Simplified install.sh / install.ps1 to drop jq dependency and the
    `gemini extensions install` step (Claude Code plugins are loaded
    automatically when .claude-plugin/plugin.json is present).
  - Simplified update.sh / update.ps1 / uninstall.sh / uninstall.ps1
    accordingly.

The hard constraints, GAQL validation rules, conversion troubleshooting
workflow, all api_examples/ scripts, and the conversions/ rulebook are
preserved verbatim from the upstream and remain Google's authored work.

